{"type": "say", "text": "To answer your first question, Riley: based on what I've confirmed so far, the regional-only reads recommendation is purely a cost optimization to avoid the ~$1,200/month in unplanned egress charges. I have not been given any information suggesting that regional-only reads would cause a correctness or availability problem for Linux/macOS build projects. That said, I can only speak to the cost data I verified this morning — I don't have visibility into whether there are any Linux/macOS projects that specifically depend on cross-region cache availability, so if Theo or the CI platform team has insight on that, it would be worth confirming."}
```

